    "q-335091": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335091",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{-3t} & (1-3t){e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & -3{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
